ummerer and Maximilian Bolingbroke and Michael Tartre and Mikhail Pak and Nathaniel J. Smith and Nikolai Nowaczyk and Nikolay Shebanov and Oleksandr Pavlyk and Per A. Brodtkorb and Perry Lee and Robert T. McGibbon and Roman Feldbauer and Sam Lewis and Sam Tygier and Scott Sievert and Sebastiano Vigna and Stefan Peterson and Surhud More and Tadeusz Pudlik and Takuya Oshima and Thomas J. Pingel and Thomas P. Robitaille and Thomas Spura and Thouis R. Jones and Tim Cera and Tim Leslie and Tiziano Zito and Tom Krauss and Utkarsh Upadhyay and Yaroslav O. Halchenko and Yoshiki Vazquez-Baeza},\n  year = {2020},\n  howpublished = {Nature Methods},\n  doi = {10.1038/s41592-019-0686-2}\n}\n\n@misc{Hunter2007,\n  title = {{Matplotlib: A 2D Graphics Environment}},\n  author = {John D. Hunter},\n  year = {2007},\n  howpublished = {Computing in Science \\& Engineering},\n  doi = {10.1109/mcse.2007.55}\n}\n\n@misc{McKinney2010,\n  title = {{Data Structures for Statistical Computing in Python}},\n  author = {Wes McKinney},\n  year = {2010},\n  howpublished = {Proceedings of the Python in Science Conferences},\n  doi = {10.25080/majora-92bf1922-00a}\n}\n\n@misc{GermanCredit,\n  title = {{Statlog (German Credit Data)}},\n  author = {Hofmann, Hans},\n  year = {1994},\n  howpublished = {UC Irvine},\n  doi = {10.24432/c5nc77}\n}\n# Global Memory Summary\n\nUse as qualitative context only; do not use as quantitative grounding source.\n\n## Recent Entries\n\n- 2026-11-07 | step=idea | scope=idea\n  - summary: Wrote Fixed-budget single-call SHAP certificates and matching rubrics. gate=kept; trigger=none; reason=Untested design only, with no new measured evidence warranting a distilled recommendation.\n  - evidence: Prompt supplies an accepted incumbent combined_score=0.9064091496251445 and correct=true, with no recent attempts or failure evidence. Named incumbent source unavailable; interface and improvement headroom unknown. No computational probes, program/evaluator runs, installations or