nBreiman2001: Random Forests\nHosmer2013: Applied Logistic Regression\nPedregosa2011: Scikit-learn: Machine Learning in Python\nHarris2020: Array programming with NumPy\nVirtanen2020: SciPy 1.0: fundamental algorithms for scientific computing in Python\nHunter2007: Matplotlib: A 2D Graphics Environment\nMcKinney2010: Data Structures for Statistical Computing in Python\nGermanCredit: Statlog (German Credit Data)\n\nLiterature-grounded claims:\n{\"claim\": \"Bibliographic context only: A Unified Approach to Interpreting Model Predictions. Not an evaluated comparator unless independently measured.\", \"citation_keys\": [\"Lundberg2017\"]}\n{\"claim\": \"Bibliographic context only: The Disagreement Problem in Explainable Machine Learning: A Practitioner's Perspective. Not an evaluated comparator unless independently measured.\", \"citation_keys\": [\"Krishna2022\"]}\n{\"claim\": \"Bibliographic context only: An empirical study of the effect of background data size on the stability of SHapley Additive exPlanations (SHAP) for deep learning models. Not an evaluated comparator unless independently measured.\", \"citation_keys\": [\"Yuan2022\"]}\n{\"claim\": \"Bibliographic context only: Provably Accurate Shapley Value Estimation via Leverage Score Sampling. Not an evaluated comparator unless independently measured.\", \"citation_keys\": [\"Musco2024\"]}\n{\"claim\": \"Bibliographic context only: True to the Model or True to the Data?. Not an evaluated comparator unless independently measured.\", \"citation_keys\": [\"Chen2020\"]}\n{\"claim\": \"Bibliographic context only: Predictive Multiplicity in Classification. Not an evaluated comparator unless independently measured.\", \"citation_keys\": [\"Marx2020\"]}\n{\"claim\": \"Bibliographic context only: On the stability of feature selection algorithms. Not an evaluated comparator unless independently measured.\", \"citation_keys\": [\"Nogueira2018\"]}\n{\"claim\": \"Bibliographic context only: A similarity measure for indefinite rankings. Not an evaluated comparator unless independently measured.\", \"citation_keys\": [\"Webber2010\"]}\n{\"claim\": \"Bibliographic context only: Retiring Adult: New Datasets for Fair Machine Learning. Not an evaluated comparator unless independently measured.\", \"citation_keys\": [\"Ding2021\"]}\n{\"claim\": \"Bibliographic context only: Revisiting Deep Learning Models for Tabular Data. Not an evaluated comparator unless independently measured.\", \"citation_keys\": [\"Gorishniy2021\"]}\n{\"claim\": \"Bibliographic context only: Consistent Individualized Feature Attribution for Tree Ensembles. Not an evaluated comparator unless independently measured.\", \"citation_keys\": [\"Lundberg2018\"]}\n{\"claim\": \"Bibliographic context only: Multilinear Extensions of Games. Not an evaluated comparator unless independently measured.\", \"citation_keys\": [\"Owen1972\"]}\n{\"claim\": \"Bibliographic context only: 17. A Value for n-Person Games. Not an evaluated comparator unless independently measured.\", \"citation_keys\": [\"Shapley1953\"]}\n{\"claim\": \"Bibliographic context only: Polynomial calculation of the Shapley value based on sampling. Not an evaluated comparator unless independently measured.\", \"citation_keys\": [\"Castro2009\"]}\n{\"claim\": \"Bibliographic context only: Probability Inequalities for Sums of Bounded Random Variables. Not an evaluated comparator unless independently measured.\", \"citation_keys\": [\"Hoeffding1963\"]}\n{\"claim\": \"Bibliographic context only: Empirical Bernstein Bounds and Sample Variance Penalization. Not an evaluated comparator unless independently measured.\", \"citation_keys\": [\"Maurer2009\"]}\n{\"claim\": \"Bibliographic context only: Bootstrap Methods: Another Look at the Jackknife. Not an evaluated comparator unless independently measured.\", \"citation_keys\": [\"Efron1979\"]}\n{\"claim\": \"Bibliographic context only: Random Forests. Not an evaluated comparator unless independently measured.\", \"citation_keys\": [\"Breiman2001\"]}\n{\"claim\": \"Bibliographic context only: Applied Logistic Regression. Not an evaluated comparator unless independently measured.\", \"citation_keys\": [\"Hosmer2013\"]}\n{\"claim\": \"Bibliographic context only: Scikit-learn: Machine Learning in Python. Not an evaluated comparator unless independently measured.\", \"citation_keys\": [\"Pedregosa2011\"]}\n{\"claim\": \"Bibliographic context only: Array programming with NumPy. Not an evaluated comparator unless independently measured.\", \"citation_keys\": [\"Harris2020\"]}\n{\"claim\": \"Bibliographic context only: SciPy 1.0: fundamental algorithms for scientific computing in Python. Not an evaluated comparator unless independently measured.\", \"citation_keys\": [\"Virtanen2020\"]}\n{\"claim\": \"Bibliographic context only: Matplotlib: A 2D Graphics Environment. Not an evaluated comparator unless independently measured.\", \"citation_keys\": [\"Hunter2007\"]}\n{\"claim\": \"Bibliographic context only: Data Structures for Statistical Computing in Python. Not an evaluated comparator unless independently measured.\", \"citation_keys\": [\"McKinney2010\"]}\n{\"claim\": \"Bibliographic context only: Statlog (German Credit Data). Not an evaluated comparator unless independently measured.\", \"citation_keys\": [\"GermanCredit\"]}\n\nWriter notes:\n[\n  \"Main-body architecture and footprint, inclusive of figures/tables: introduction and early overview 1.25 pages; related work 0.65; fixed-game estimand and metrics 1.0; model-specific computation 1.4; experimental and statistical protocol 1.05; results and component comparison 2.0; limitations and interpretation 0.9; conclusion 0.25. Total target 8.5 pages under the supplied 8–9-page venue rule. An 8-page body must fill at least 75% of its final page. Use remaining space for equations, reference limitations and fair comparison, not more search history or oversized figures.\",\n  \"Two compact main tables complement the figures: an experimental-design table with dataset version, split, feature count, background, model, reference type and cap; and a final-reliability table with condition-specific reference agreement, stored conditional intervals at their actual scope, top-three/sign agreement and repeat consistency. Keep global integrity checks in a short adjacent paragraph rather than relabeling them as predictive accuracy.\",\n  \"Template inspection: .codex/skills/write-paper-standalone/templates/iclr/paper.tex uses article plus paper,times; paper.sty specifies 5.5in text width and 9in text height, with no two-column layout. Full_width means one full text column, not a two-column float. Do not use the template's sample title or author block; omit identifying material and final-copy author mode for the double-blind paper while preserving required template infrastructure.\",\n  \"Final qualification must remain auditable through final.qualification.status, final.qualification.outcome, and final.qualification.correct. In this run they report completed, qualified, and true. Reader-facing disclosure should say the evaluation met its documented completeness and analytic-control requirements, not that scientific reliability was certified. Review/audit/revision must preserve this scope; if later authoritative evidence reports failed qualification, disclose it explicitly and do not diagnose performance, validity or adaptivity causes without criterion evidence.\",\n  \"The final tested method is primary. Private-only source bridge: best_program_manifest.json names the recoverable third configuration; final_evaluation independently records final outcomes. No downstream_study or study.* records exist, so do not publish search selection scores, score differences, attempt totals or an alleged original baseline win. The memory-only incumbent score is not a comparator.\",\n  \"Use final.evidence.episodes for the main per-condition results and final.metric.* for aggregate checks. Private-only: result.top_program_01/02/03 identify the full, forest-enabled, and sampled configurations; follow each all_programs evaluation_evidence.episodes array for development comparisons. Those source IDs' scalar values alone do not establish an ablation. Trace the array path and inspected source change in downstream claim mappings; do not invent missing grounding IDs.\",\n  \"Data regime: German has 20 supplied scalar feature groups and final retained splits 300 train/100 validation/100 explanation; ACS has 10 groups and 20000/6667/6667. Only the first 16 explanation instances and first 16 training-background rows are used in the final study. These split counts are from the inspected resource records, not measurements of generalization. Name ACSIncome-2024-RELSHIPP explicitly, retain the provenance adapter and the search/final content-disjointness construction, and do not call it bit-identical historical ACSIncome.\",\n  \"Frozen model conditions are logistic regression (lbfgs, max_iter=500, tol=1e-7) and forests (64 trees, max_depth=6, n_jobs=1). Final episode seeds are 104729, 130363 and 155921; each has caps 64/256/1024 and six candidate calls per cap. Fixed instances recur across episodes; model randomness can differ for forests, while logistic fitting may be deterministic. Do not count these as 48 independent queried people or treat six deterministic repeats as six independent fidelity observations.\",\n  \"Use the exact evaluator definitions: reference agreement is reciprocal normalized L1 error with a 0.001 denominator floor; top-three compares absolute attribution sets with original-column tie breaking; sign agreement covers all coordinates with an absolute 1e-8 zero threshold; normalized efficiency residual is capped at one with a 0.001 denominator floor. These are not user-validated reliability thresholds, calibration scores, causal correctness, or fairness assessments.\",\n  \"Existing 95% bootstrap intervals resample 16 instance-level agreement summaries after averaging candidate repeats and caps, conditional on one model/reference, with 1000 resamples and seed 84017. They are not per-cap intervals, do not incorporate approximate-reference error, and cannot be averaged into a new interval. Show per-episode points for budget-specific comparisons and label any descriptive range as a range, not a confidence interval. Do not manufacture significance claims.\",\n  \"German references average two 4096-coalition library estimates; abs(first-second)/2 is a disagreement proxy, not a confidence bound. ACS references enumerate all 2^10 coalitions. The candidate's nonforest exhaustive dispatch activates when cap >= 2^d-2, so ACS logistic cap 1024 does not demonstrate the quadrature branch. Forest dispatch precedes that check. Branch acceptance/rejection counts, certificate coverage, and total quadrature error certificates are not recorded; deterministic output does not recover those missing facts.\",\n  \"Model-agnostic library comparators use prediction queries; the proposed computation receives model parameters. A nominal sampled-coalition cap is not a matched arithmetic, wall-clock or information-access budget. Actual baseline prediction rows are recorded; candidate per-call timing and comparable prediction-cost diagnostics are not. Report measured total time only in its correct all-work scope; do not substitute the source task's estimated CPU-hour budget for observed usage.\",\n  \"Current sources support a bounded engineering/methodology contribution, not first-ever exact tree attribution or first-ever SHAP stability analysis. The bibliography is a noisy retrieved candidate pool with metadata-level provenance, not proof every source has been read. Use only relevant permitted primary works actually consulted and keys present in references.bib, starting from Lundberg2017AUA, Musco2024ProvablyAS, and appropriate tree-attribution records after verification. Missing Owen/empirical-Bernstein/semantics sources cannot be replaced with invented citations or unsupported novelty claims; keep nonessential certificate theory out of the central contribution.\",\n  \"Do not perform broad reliability-literature discovery or attempt to identify the prohibited paper. No external paper pages were accessed during this strategy stage, and no prohibited encounter was identified here. Do not infer that prior retrieval was fully reviewed or contamination-free merely from its presence. Any actual prohibited encounter must be stopped and recorded with URL and extent of reading.\",\n  \"All main quantitative views are descriptive transformations of retained measured arrays, with scripts and source pointers preserved. Do not invent runs, confidence bands, missing measurements, calibration, background-size sensitivity, latency distributions, acceptance coverage, alternative datasets or tested external TreeSHAP/leverage-score baselines. Unscored or unrun alternatives remain missing evidence, never measured losses. Standalone forest/logistic validation scripts being present does not establish their execution.\",\n  \"Use vector-first matplotlib outputs: preserve plotting source/data and export both PDF and PNG, PNG at 300 DPI; LaTeX must prefer PDF whenever it exists. A raster-only full-width figure must be regenerated from source at >=2400px wide, and any column/partial-width raster at >=1200px; never upscale. The concept-figure workflow is orchestrator-owned, uses one editable draw.io overview, and does not itself promise PDF export. Prefer a PDF exported from its vector source when available; otherwise require the full-width raster minimum and a recorded prompt/source manifest. Do not invoke image generation during strategy planning.\",\n  \"Use consistent method colors: gray for one-shot library, orange for split-cap averaging, blue for structure-aware computation. Use gray for the disabled component and blue for the enabled component in development comparisons, explicitly label that local contrast, and preserve meanings in legends. Distinguish reference quality with text rather than reassigning method colors. Avoid decorative failure/success icons that imply unmeasured thresholds.\",\n  \"Keep the main conclusion conditional: one call is adequate for the observed same-game top-three/sign/reference-agreement criteria in these evaluated conditions, not universally adequate as a reason for a prediction. No task-specific acceptable-error threshold or human decision study was prespecified. Small fixed query sets, fixed nonrepresentative background choice, scalar categorical encoding, approximate German references, unrecorded branch diagnostics, and no human/causal/background-shift validation must appear in the main limitations, not only the supplement.\",\n  \"After the main body, flush floats, place references, then clear the page and use appendix plus a Supplementary Information section with substantive subsections. Add a separate LLM Usage section, preferably there, disclosing the documented roles in ideation, code preparation and paper planning/writing without inventing model identifiers or human review. Follow any supplied authoritative appendix rankings later without retroactively changing this strategy or hiding central evidence.\",\n  \"This is a framing artifact only. Do not create paper.tex or claims_grounding.json here, do not run final-paper validation, and do not claim official-template provenance or submission readiness merely because the supplied local style was inspected. Downstream writing must retain venue anonymization, actual checklist obligations, figure/script traceability, and all evaluation limitations.\"\n]\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
